# mc.homelab.com — public landing page for the Minecraft server.
# Game ports (25565 Java, 19132 Bedrock) bypass Cloudflare entirely by
# design (the VPS publishes them directly, see services/mc/
# docker-compose.yml), so this vhost is just a human-readable landing
# page so anyone hitting https://mc.homelab.com in a browser gets
# connect info instead of a 404.
#
# TLS: Let's Encrypt DNS-01 via the Cloudflare DNS plugin. mc.homelab.com
# is DNS-only at CF (the CF proxy would break the game ports), so the
# HTTP-01 challenge can't reach the origin over port 80. DNS-01 instead
# lets Caddy drop a _acme-challenge TXT record at CF over HTTPS using
# the token in CF_API_TOKEN, LE validates it, and Caddy stores the cert
# under /data (persistent) for automatic renewal. No port 80 needed.
# The other vhosts in this Caddyfile use the CF Origin CA (channels
# 67-72) shared wildcard cert, so the mc.homelab.com vhost explicitly
# opts into its own ACME cert instead of importing `tls_keys` — this
# prevents the wildcard cert from being served as a SNI fallback for
# this hostname and lets the ACME automation policy take precedence.

https://mc.homelab.com {
    tls {
        dns cloudflare {env.CF_API_TOKEN}
    }
    import compress
    header {
        Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
        X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
    }
    @root path /
    respond @root `ok


Server IP: 137.74.166.131
Java:     mc.homelab.com:25565  (Paper, latest stable)
Bedrock:  mc.homelab.com:19132  (Geyser + Floodgate, TCP+UDP)


Dashboard (Tailscale-only): https://server.homelab.com/mc
`
    respond "not found" 404
}
